    "steps": [
      {
        "text": "Insert a batch log record with STATUS = 'PROCESSING' and START_DT (log message no. 1). Get the watermark = WATERMARK_TO of the last F1 run with STATUS = 'SUCCESS'.",
        "children": [
          "If no successful run exists, use the initial cut-off parameter (value TBD at go-live).",
          "If the parameter is not set, log message no. 4. Stop."
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Retrieve the Customer Order Dates in TB_R_CI_PENDING_ORDER_DT with STATUS = 'P', ordered by ORDER_DT ascending (GD-05)."
      },
      {
        "text": "Retrieve H0202 rows with DEMAND_HISTORY_UPDATE_CD = '06' (see 4.1):",
        "children": [
          "Group A: all rows of the pending ORDER_DT from step 2, regardless of the watermark.",
          "Group B: rows with CREATE_DT > watermark whose ORDER_DT is not pending (delta).",
          "New watermark = MAX(CREATE_DT) of the rows read; unchanged if nothing was read.",
          "If no row is found, log message no. 5 and go to step 7."
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Process ORDER_DT one by one: Group A first, then Group B, oldest ORDER_DT first. Check every ORDER_PART_NO of the ORDER_DT against MASTER_CANDIDATE_PART (see 4.2)."
      },
      {
        "text": "If any part is not Active: do not insert any row of this ORDER_DT. Insert the date into TB_R_CI_PENDING_ORDER_DT with STATUS = 'P', or update the existing record (log message no. 6). Proceed to the next ORDER_DT.",
        "children": [
          "Other ORDER_DT that pass the check are still processed (business rejection, not a batch failure)."
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "If all parts are Active: insert every row whose unique key does not exist in TB_R_CUSTOMER_INSTRUCTION (see 4.3). Skip existing keys (log message no. 8).",
        "children": [
          "If the ORDER_DT was pending, set its STATUS = 'R' (Released) (log message no. 7).",
          "If an insert fails, log message no. 10, roll back all changes of this run and go to the error end."
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "When all ORDER_DT are processed, commit. Update the batch log: STATUS = 'SUCCESS', counts, WATERMARK_TO = new watermark, END_DT (log message no. 2). Return success so that F2 starts.",
        "children": [
          "Error end: STATUS = 'ERROR', WATERMARK_TO = watermark from step 1 (not moved), END_DT. Return error; F2 to F4 are not executed (GD-10)."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
