  "func_desc_layout": "two",
  "func_desc": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "4. DESCRIPTION",
      "level": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "F1 is the first function of the daily Case Consolidation job. It copies new crossdock customer order lines from H0202 into TB_R_CUSTOMER_INSTRUCTION. It only inserts; cancel (F2), PO mapping (F3) and case assignment (F4) update the rows later.",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "Prerequisite: the H0202 load from TOPAS is finished before 05:00 (TBD).",
        "Prerequisite: Crossdock Part List master (MASTER_CANDIDATE_PART) is maintained in Crossdock Master Setting."
      ],
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "4.1 Data Selection (GD-02, GD-03, GD-05)",
      "level": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "Source condition: DEMAND_HISTORY_UPDATE_CD = '06'. Other codes (for example '07') are not read.",
        "Group A - pending dates: all '06' rows whose ORDER_DT has STATUS = 'P' in TB_R_CI_PENDING_ORDER_DT, regardless of CREATE_DT. Processed first, oldest ORDER_DT first.",
        "Group B - delta: '06' rows with CREATE_DT > watermark and ORDER_DT not pending.",
        "Watermark = WATERMARK_TO of the last SUCCESS F1 run. The new watermark is MAX(CREATE_DT) of the rows read and is saved only when the run succeeds.",
        "Rejected rows do not block the watermark, because their ORDER_DT is kept in the pending table and read again as Group A.",
        "CREATE_DT data type in H0202 is TBD (the extract shows text in Oracle format); compare as timestamp."
      ],
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "4.2 Part Status Validation (GD-04) - log message no. 6",
      "level": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "Every ORDER_PART_NO of the ORDER_DT must exist in MASTER_CANDIDATE_PART with PART_STATUS = 'Active' at the batch run date. A part that is not registered is treated as not Active (Proposed).",
        "Which MASTER_CANDIDATE_PART period is read is TBD.",
        "Rejection unit is the whole ORDER_DT: all customers, all destinations and all parts of that date. No row of the date is inserted.",
        "This is a business rejection: the batch continues with the other ORDER_DT and ends with SUCCESS."
      ],
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Example (dummy data):",
      "level": 1,
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "level": 1,
      "row_lines": "all",
      "columns": [
        {
          "title": "ORDER_DT",
          "width": 8
        },
        {
          "title": "Dest",
          "width": 4
        },
        {
          "title": "Part",
          "width": 6
        },
        {
          "title": "Part status",
          "width": 7
        },
        {
          "title": "Result",
          "width": 20
        }
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "09-Oct-26",
          "TH",
          "Part A",
          "Active",
          "Held (date pending)"
        ],
        [
          "09-Oct-26",
          "JP",
          "Part B",
          "Inactive",
          "Held (date pending)"
        ],
        [
          "09-Oct-26",
          "PH",
          "Part A",
          "Active",
          "Held (date pending)"
        ],
        [
          "10-Oct-26",
          "TH",
          "Part A",
          "Active",
          "Inserted"
        ],
        [
          "10-Oct-26",
          "PH",
          "Part C",
          "Active",
          "Inserted"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "4.3 Duplicate Prevention (GD-06, GD-07)",
      "level": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "Unique key: CUSTOMER_CD + CUSTOMER_ORDER_NO + ORDER_DT + DESTINATION_CD + ORDER_PART_NO + DETAILED_ITEM_NO. SERIAL_NO is not used.",
        "A key that already exists in TB_R_CUSTOMER_INSTRUCTION is skipped; its quantities are not updated (log message no. 8, counted in SKIPPED_ROWS).",
        "If the same key appears more than once in the rows read, insert the row with the latest CREATE_DT and log message no. 9 (Proposed).",
        "Quantity corrections made in H0202 for an existing key are handled by manual injection (GD-11)."
      ],
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "4.4 Initial Values (GD-08)",
      "level": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "level": 1,
      "row_lines": "all",
      "columns": [
        {
          "title": "Column",
          "width": 20
        },
        {
          "title": "Value at F1",
          "width": 16
        },
        {
          "title": "Changed by",
          "width": 10
        }
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "CROSS_DOCK_QTY",
          "From H0202",
          "Never"
        ],
        [
          "ORDER_QTY",
          "Same as CROSS_DOCK_QTY",
          "F2"
        ],
        [
          "CANCEL_H0253_QTY",
          "NULL",
          "F2"
        ],
        [
          "ORDER_STATUS",
          "NULL",
          "F2"
        ],
        [
          "DELETED_FLAG",
          "'N'",
          "F2"
        ],
        [
          "PO_NUMBER, PO_QTY, REMAINING_ORDER_QTY",
          "NULL",
          "F3"
        ],
        [
          "CASE_NUMBER",
          "NULL",
          "F4"
        ],
        [
          "ASN_NUMBER",
          "NULL",
          "ASN creation"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "4.5 Transaction and Error Handling (GD-10)",
      "level": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "All inserts and pending-table changes of one run are committed together at step 7.",
        "Any technical error (database connection, insert failure, unexpected error) rolls back everything; WATERMARK_TO is not moved; the job does not start F2 to F4.",
        "The batch log record is written in its own transaction so that the ERROR status remains after the rollback."
      ],
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "4.6 Out of Scope of F1",
      "level": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "Pcs/case multiple check and hold of non-multiple dates: F3, per ORDER_DT + DESTINATION_CD + PART, pcs/case from Crossdock Master Setting (GD-09).",
        "Cancel from H0253: F2.",
        "Manual injection of corrected quantities and of dates held for a long time (GD-11)."
      ],
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "4.7 Open Points",
      "level": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "bullets",
      "items": [
        "Batch ID, MSG IDs and the initial cut-off watermark at go-live.",
        "MASTER_CANDIDATE_PART period to read, and whether an unregistered part is treated as not Active.",
        "Late rows: when rows of an ORDER_DT are already inserted and a later row of the same date has a part that is not Active, the earlier rows stay in TB_R_CUSTOMER_INSTRUCTION; only the new rows are held. Confirm.",
        "Physical data types of TB_R_CUSTOMER_INSTRUCTION follow H0202; confirm lengths.",
        "SPLIT_SEQ column and key extension depend on the F3 design."
      ],
      "level": 1
    }
  ],
